document.description:
The visual's whole JSON document, valid for its type. Rules and an example per type:
- bar: orientation is vertical. mode is grouped or stacked. Each data row is an object whose keys are exactly the xKey and each series key. Series values are numbers. xKey values are strings. No other keys. series has 1 to 6 items. data has at most 500 rows. Optional references: up to 6 items, each { value, label } for a flat line at a number (a value reference may take axis right when a series is on the right axis) or { at, label } for a marker at a category. A series may have as line (drawn as a line, never stacked); such a series may have dashed true and axis right. Keep at least one bar series. Example: {"orientation":"vertical","mode":"grouped","xKey":"month","series":[{"key":"revenue","label":"Revenue"},{"key":"cost","label":"Cost"}],"data":[{"month":"Jan","revenue":120,"cost":80},{"month":"Feb","revenue":140,"cost":90}]}
- bar-horizontal: orientation is horizontal. mode is grouped or stacked. Each data row is an object whose keys are exactly the xKey and each series key. Series values are numbers. xKey values are strings. No other keys. Optional references: up to 6 items, each { value, label } for a flat line at a number or { at, label } for a marker at a category. Example: {"orientation":"horizontal","mode":"grouped","xKey":"month","series":[{"key":"revenue","label":"Revenue"},{"key":"cost","label":"Cost"}],"data":[{"month":"Jan","revenue":120,"cost":80},{"month":"Feb","revenue":140,"cost":90}]}
- line: curve is linear, monotone, or step. Each data row is an object whose keys are exactly the xKey and each series key. Series values are numbers. xKey values are strings. No other keys. Optional references: up to 6 items, each { value, label } for a flat line at a number (a value reference may take axis right when a series is on the right axis) or { at, label } for a marker at a category. A series may have dashed true. A series may have axis left or right; keep at least one series on the left. Example: {"xKey":"date","curve":"monotone","series":[{"key":"users","label":"Users"}],"data":[{"date":"2026-01","users":10}]}
- area: Same row rules as line. stacked is a boolean. Each data row is an object whose keys are exactly the xKey and each series key. Series values are numbers. xKey values are strings. No other keys. Optional references: up to 6 items, each { value, label } for a flat line at a number or { at, label } for a marker at a category. A series may have dashed true. Example: {"xKey":"date","curve":"monotone","stacked":false,"series":[{"key":"users","label":"Users"}],"data":[{"date":"2026-01","users":10}]}
- pie: Each data row is an object whose keys are exactly nameKey and valueKey. nameKey values are strings. valueKey values are numbers greater than or equal to 0. At most 24 slices. donut is a boolean. Example: {"nameKey":"category","valueKey":"amount","donut":true,"data":[{"category":"New","amount":40},{"category":"Returning","amount":60}]}
- kpi: label is a string, value is a number, format is number, compact, or percent. Optional prefix, suffix, delta, deltaFormat (number or percent), deltaLabel, and trend (up to 60 numbers, oldest first, in the same unit as value). No other keys. Example: {"label":"MRR","value":12840,"format":"number","prefix":"$","suffix":"","delta":0.12,"deltaFormat":"percent","deltaLabel":"vs last month"}
- table: columns has 1 to 12 entries with key, label, align left or right, and format text, number, or percent. data has at most 200 rows. Each row's keys are column keys and hrefKey keys. Cell values are strings, numbers, or null. A text column may have statuses, a map from cell text to good, warn, or bad (1 to 20 entries). A number or percent column may have rules: 1 to 6 items, each { below or atLeast, status }; the first match wins. A text column may have hrefKey, a row key whose value (an http or https URL, null or empty) links the cell. Example: {"columns":[{"key":"name","label":"Name","align":"left","format":"text"},{"key":"amount","label":"Amount","align":"right","format":"number"}],"data":[{"name":"Acme","amount":10}]}
- markdown: The only key is source, a string of at most 20000 characters. Example: {"source":"## Notes\n\n- Pipeline is up\n- See [status](https://example.com)"}
- scatter: xKey and yKey values are numbers. labelKey is optional and its values are strings. Each row's keys are exactly xKey, yKey, and labelKey when labelKey is present. At most 500 points. Example: {"xKey":"price","yKey":"units","labelKey":"label","data":[{"price":10,"units":3,"label":"A"}]}
- funnel: Each row's keys are exactly nameKey and valueKey. Names are strings. Values are numbers greater than or equal to 0. data may be empty or have at most 12 stages. Keep array order. Example: {"nameKey":"stage","valueKey":"count","data":[{"stage":"Visit","count":1000},{"stage":"Signup","count":400},{"stage":"Paid","count":80}]}
- gauge: label is a string. value, min, and max are numbers with min less than max. suffix is an optional string. No other keys. Example: {"label":"Utilization","value":72,"min":0,"max":100,"suffix":"%"}
- map: region is world, us-states or us-counties. idKey and valueKey name the row fields; labelKey is optional. format is number (default), compact or percent; prefix and suffix are optional strings. Each data row's keys are exactly idKey, valueKey and labelKey when set. The idKey value is a region code: for world an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code such as DE (alpha-3 accepted), for us-states a USPS code such as CA (two-digit FIPS accepted), for us-counties a five-digit county FIPS code such as 06037 (the 2017 county lines, leading zero kept); case is ignored. At most one row per region; a code with no shape on the map (Puerto Rico and the territories on us-states; territories drawn as part of their country on world; Connecticut's planning regions and Alaska's Chugach and Copper River on us-counties) is refused with the region's name. valueKey values are numbers. Example: {"region":"world","idKey":"country","valueKey":"signups","format":"number","data":[{"country":"US","signups":412},{"country":"GB","signups":138},{"country":"DE","signups":96},{"country":"IN","signups":87},{"country":"CA","signups":64},{"country":"BR","signups":41},{"country":"AU","signups":33},{"country":"JP","signups":19}]}
- progress: nameKey and valueKey name the row fields; give either maxKey, the row field holding each row's own target, or max, one target for every row (a number greater than 0), never both. format is number (default), compact or percent; prefix and suffix are optional strings (up to 80 characters) applied to the value and the target. Each data row's keys are exactly nameKey, valueKey and maxKey when set. Names are strings of 1 to 80 characters, one row per name. valueKey values are numbers greater than or equal to 0; maxKey values are numbers greater than 0. data has at most 20 rows, drawn in the order listed. Optional rules: 1 to 6 items, each { below or atLeast, status good, warn or bad }; the first match wins, judged on the share done (value divided by target, so 1 means the target is met). An append merges by name; keepLast does not apply, and an append that would make more than 20 rows is refused. Example: {"nameKey":"project","valueKey":"done","maxKey":"total","format":"number","rules":[{"below":0.5,"status":"bad"},{"below":0.9,"status":"warn"},{"atLeast":0.9,"status":"good"}],"data":[{"project":"Website","done":34,"total":40},{"project":"Mobile app","done":12,"total":30},{"project":"Docs","done":22,"total":20}]}
- status-grid: nameKey and statusKey name the row fields; noteKey and hrefKey are optional and name two more. The four keys must be different from each other. Each data row's keys are exactly nameKey, statusKey, noteKey when set and hrefKey when set. Names are strings of 1 to 80 characters, one row per name. statuses is optional, a map from your status words to good, warn or bad (1 to 20 entries, words of 1 to 200 characters); with it a status is any string up to 200 characters and a word not in the map draws grey (no status), without it a status is good, warn, bad or an empty string. A note is a string of up to 80 characters or null. A link is an http or https URL of up to 2048 characters, null or an empty string for no link. data has at most 200 items, drawn in the order listed. An append merges by name; keepLast does not apply, and an append that would make more than 200 rows is refused. Example: {"nameKey":"site","statusKey":"patch","statuses":{"Patched":"good","Pending":"warn","Not patched":"bad"},"noteKey":"version","hrefKey":"admin","data":[{"site":"shop.example.com","patch":"Patched","version":"6.4.2","admin":"https://shop.example.com/wp-admin"},{"site":"blog.example.com","patch":"Not patched","version":"6.1.0","admin":"https://blog.example.com/wp-admin"}]}
- heatmap: layout is grid or calendar. A grid names xKey, yKey and valueKey and must not have dateKey; a calendar names dateKey and valueKey and must not have xKey or yKey. The keys of a layout must be different from each other. format is number (default), compact or percent; prefix and suffix are optional strings (up to 80 characters) applied to the value. Each data row's keys are exactly the layout's keys: xKey, yKey and valueKey on a grid, dateKey and valueKey on a calendar. On a grid x and y values are strings of 1 to 80 characters ("07", not 7), each x and y pair appears once, there are at most 60 distinct x values and 60 distinct y values, x runs across and y down in the order first seen. On a calendar dates are real days written YYYY-MM-DD, each date appears once, and the dates span at most 366 days from the earliest to the latest (weeks start on Monday). valueKey values are numbers; a cell with no row is drawn as no data. data has at most 1000 items. An append merges by cell (the x and y pair) on a grid and by date on a calendar; keepLast does not apply, and an append that would make more than 1000 rows is refused. The latest date sets a calendar's 366-day window: an append drops the days before it and counts them in dropped, and an append that would push every stored day out of it is refused, so a mistyped year cannot erase the calendar. Calendar example: {"layout":"calendar","dateKey":"date","valueKey":"minutes","suffix":" min","data":[{"date":"2026-11-23","minutes":45},{"date":"2026-11-24","minutes":30}]} Example: {"layout":"grid","xKey":"hour","yKey":"day","valueKey":"kwh","suffix":" kWh","data":[{"day":"Mon","hour":"07","kwh":1.4},{"day":"Mon","hour":"08","kwh":0.9}]}
